	affiliations = {Department of Information Technology, R V College of Engineering, Karnataka, Bangalore, India},
	abstract = {As DDoS attacks continue to grow in strength it is crucial to implement IDS systems to improve network service availability and stability especially when dealing with cloud platforms, like OpenStack. This study introduces an intrusion detection system along with SIEM to promptly and accurately identify DDoS attacks within the OpenStack infrastructure. The Suricata, an open-source intrusion detection system in collaboration with the Wazuh security monitoring platform at free cost. Initially Suricata is set up. Configured within the OpenStack to analyze network traffic and detect patterns associated with DDoS attacks. Specific rules for DDoS detection are created for Suricata encompassing known attack signatures and malicious patterns. This article aims to demonstrate how easily one can begin using Wazuh Cluster for log management and security event correlation, which integrates seamlessly with Suricata to address threats automatically. Wazuh is the central hub for gathering, evaluating and handling Suricata notifications. Using the guidance of the recommended intelligent IDS, OpenStack administrators will be able to rapidly identify assaults in real time and take appropriate action in response to any potential DDoS threats. The purpose of effective DDoS attack detection within the OpenStack, the recommended approach prevents OpenStack infrastructures from DDoS attacks while leveraging the capabilities of open-source technology to sustain the integrity of the services delivered.  © 2024 Author(s).},
